Z||000010||TOM||12-29-1999||02:45 AM||||The 308 was too real. My mom worked on the show and I got a ride in it once.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||12-29-1999||03:20 AM||||Was she one of the actresses?  Are we in the midst of a pseudo-celebrity? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  What about autographs?  Maybe she worked on the cars?  That would be even cooler, IMHO!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Tom88gt||12-29-1999||02:14 PM||||The kit car article said Meras were 87s & 88s.  I saw one once at a Knott's Berry Farm Kit Car show.  The owner had a big sign saying "this is NOT a kit".  But the Mera molds were sold and are now available as a kit.  To me, it was just a turn key kit and not worth anymore than a similar quality 308 kit on an 87-88 V-6.  I beleive the C&C t-tops were done by the same company. ||||reg||1
